  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Bishkek Public Transport Project Extension</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The EBRD supports further improvements of the public transport system in the  city of Bishkek (the &quot;City&quot;) by extending a sovereign loan of up to EUR 5.0  million (provided in two tranches) to the Kyrgyz Republic. The loan funds will  be on-lent to the City for the benefit of Municipal Enterprise &quot;Bishkek  Trolleybus Department&quot; (the &quot;Company&quot;). The loan is co-financed by a EUR 2.9  million grant from the EBRD Shareholder Special Fund (also provided in two  tranches). The proceeds of the loan and grant will be used to purchase 49 new  low-floor trolleybuses (the &quot;Project&quot;).  The Project&apos;s purpose is to contribute further to expanding electric transport  in the City. In addition, a Public Transport Development Strategy (focused on  enhanced regulatory framework) will be prepared to support the implementation  of the new urban transport master plan in the City.</narrative>
  </description>
